\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, when we have not any light,
\par And mothers are asleep,
\par Then through the stillness of the night
\par Thy little children keep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When shadows haunt the quiet room,
\par Help us to understand
\par That Thou art with us through the gloom,
\par To hold us by the hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And though we do not always see
\par The holy angels near,
\par O may we trust ourselves to Thee,
\par Nor have one foolish fear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. So in the morning may we wake,
\par When wakes the kindly sun,
\par More loving for our Father's sake
\par To teach unloving one.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

